{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-crossroads-continent/1546108-inktober-postings-and-story-with-art-redux-4","id":1546108,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #4","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Crossroads Continent"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-18T19:03:24-08:00","id":1546108,"title":"Inktober postings and story with art Redux #4","content":"Inktober Redux4: In the same merchants and craftsmen area that the sea elf got her new boots in, Hugh Vandalay sold a bunch of the gems and other valuables the crew recovered from the ancient chamber of the necromancer. The same gnomish jeweler actually dipped his pen in ink and sketched out a map of the northeastern part of the Crossroads Continent so that they could find their way to the north where Hugh has heard that worshipers of his little-known god still live.<br /> <br /> With that, they decide to sail back along the coast to the delta where several rivers combine to empty the sea, and sail up through the swampy lowlands to rivers that can take them further north (rather than risk the dangers of heading east and then north along the coast). Now with two damaged small ships, Captain M'udd is really having fun!<br /> <br /> The party has a number of encounters as they work their way through the overgrown, marshy, forest including ruins, the remains of a knightly hydra-hunting party, several tribes of Lizardmen, huge hulking humanoid mounds of shambling vegetation, and other signs of the predatory nature of the swamp, but eventually they can see a column or pillar through the leaves and it looks like the river is taking them straight towards it!<br /> <br /> Yes it did, and the river, in fact, splits and in the middle they see a settlement, with docks, and huts and cabins, maybe even caves carved back into the rising land. It even looks like a small figure is waving them in to one of the docks! (This location was one I made up to provide the party with a source for missions and reasons to explore further into the jungle. And a place to rest and where they could develop relationships with the inhabitants. More on those in tomorrow's post. The crew didn't have to choose to stay at the trading post, but I created enough that if they did, there were potential storylines to play through and build up further).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}